# Access-widener TEMPLATE for the Fabric nodes — the counterpart of
# src/main/resources/META-INF/accesstransformer_mojmap.cfg, which serves Forge and NeoForge.
#
# This file is NOT a valid access widener as it stands and is never shipped: it carries no
# header, and the `#?` directives below are not widener syntax. build-logic/AccessWidener.kt
# reads it once per node, evaluates each directive against that node's MC version, and writes
# a real widener into build/generated/ with the right header namespace (`named` below 26,
# `official` on the loom-no-remap 26.x line).
#
# It lives OUTSIDE src/ on purpose: Stonecutter registers `.accesswidener` as a `#`-comment
# file type and would try to preprocess it at stonecutterPrepare, and a widener's header has
# to be the literal first line, which no comment-based gate can guarantee.
#
# TWO RULES FOR EDITING THIS FILE (both learned the hard way in the sibling AlexsMobsContinued
# tree, and both cost a failed build there):
#
#   1. A FIELD entry must carry the field's DESCRIPTOR; an access-transformer line must not.
#      A METHOD entry carries its full descriptor too. Getting one wrong is a build failure,
#      not a no-op — loom's validateAccessWidener refuses to build.
#
#   2. Pre-flight EVERY version before touching a node:
#          python3 scripts/aw_check.py
#      It javaps the unpatched Mojmap jars for all 22 planned Fabric versions and reports any
#      entry whose class, member or descriptor moved. An AT that matches nothing is silently
#      ignored on Forge; an AW that matches nothing stops the build.
#
# THREE CONVERSIONS THAT ARE NOT ONE-TO-ONE WITH THE AT:
#
#   * `public-f X f`  ->  `accessible field` PLUS `mutable field` (two lines; AW splits what
#     the AT's `-f` suffix bundles).
#   * `public-f X *`  ->  every member spelled out. AW has NO wildcard.
#   * A PRIVATE method the mod OVERRIDES must be `extendable`, never `accessible`.
#     `accessible` on a private method is `makePublic(makeFinalIfPrivate(...))` — it makes the
#     method final, forbidding the override. `extendable` is `makeProtected(removeFinal(...))`
#     and rewrites the in-class INVOKESPECIAL call site to INVOKEVIRTUAL, which is exactly what
#     an override needs. (Read out of net.fabricmc:access-widener:2.1.0's bytecode —
#     AccessWidener$MethodAccess and AccessWidenerClassVisitor$AccessWidenerMethodVisitor.)
#     Two members here are in that position: Entity#collide and AbstractArrow#startFalling.
#     Because of it, NEITHER needs a `//? if !fabric` gate or a Fabric-only dispatch mixin —
#     the seven overrides in this tree compile unchanged on all three loaders.
#
# Mixins do not need entries here: @Shadow/@Accessor/@Invoker reach anything. The exception is
# a @Shadow field declared WIDER than the target's, or one that is written when the target is
# final — BiomeSource#possibleBiomes is exactly that, which is why it is below.

accessible	field	net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity	jumping	Z

accessible	method	net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap	randomState	()Lnet/minecraft/world/level/levelgen/RandomState;

